WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:06.370
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:13.910
The reading from the Sinaxadion for September 16th, on which we commemorate the Holy and

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:20.130
Great Martyr, Ophemia, the All-Famed.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:26.330
On the 16th of the month, we celebrate the memory of the Holy and Great Martyr, Ophemia

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.850
of Calcedon.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:37.570
Great Ophemia lived at Calcedon in the reign of Diocletian in the years 284 through 305.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:43.290
Her parents were rich and devout and brought her up in the love of Christ.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:51.530
At that time, Priscus became Pro-Consul of Asia and ordered all the inhabitants of the province

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:58.450
to come to Calcedon to celebrate the feast of his God, under pain of death.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:04.450
Whereupon the Christians fled in small groups to isolated houses or to the deserts in

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:10.410
order to escape the tyrant and safeguard their faith.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:16.930
Saint Ophemia was among those who went into hiding, and by her virtue and wisdom shown

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:21.450
as a bright star amid her 49 companions.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:27.370
They were soon discovered and brought before the Pro-Consul who tried to persuade them

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:33.050
to sacrifice by flattering their youth and good sense.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:38.930
Do not waste your time and your words on us, the saints answered him.

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:46.650
We are people endowed with reason for whom it would be the greatest disgrace to abandon

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:55.970
the one true God, the maker of heaven and earth, in order to worship dumb, senseless idols.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:02:00.090
We are not afraid of the torments you threaten us with.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:08.360
They will be easy for us to bear, and will show you the power of our God.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:17.280
These words enraged the Pro-Consul, and he had Ophemia and her companions tortured continuously

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.840
for twenty days.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:26.240
Then finding their faith completely unshaken and seeing that Ophemia was the leading spirit

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:33.080
of the group, he ordered her limbs to be crushed by iron wheels.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:40.200
But the martyr called upon the help of God and was discovered to be completely unscathed.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:46.440
Then she was cast into a furnace with flames forty feet high.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:53.640
But God came to Ophemia's aid there also and sent an angel who drew the flames away from

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.480
her.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:03:03.640
Even this miracle, the executioner's victor and sostenies turned to Christ and died as

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:09.240
martyrs some days later at the teeth of the beasts.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:15.960
The saint had many more torments to endure, from which God each time delivered her, showing

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:24.360
how much stronger grace is than any torture the malice of men can devise.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:30.660
In the end she was thrown to the beasts and gave up her soul to God through the mere

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:34.280
bite of a bear.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:39.320
When the persecution of Diocletian ended, the Christians laid Saint Ephemias relics in

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:44.680
a golden sarcophagus, placed within a church that was dedicated to her.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:51.760
On her feast day there would flow from her tomb a stream of fresh blood, having a heavenly

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.120
scent.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:58.000
The miraculous rejection of the tomb of the heretics during the Council of Calcedon

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:07.360
in the year 451 also occurred at her shrine, see the commemoration for July 11th.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.520
Her relics attracted crowds of pilgrims for centuries.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:18.840
They were translated to Constantinople in the year 616 at the time of the Persian invasions

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:27.080
and remain intact to this day in the church of the Patriarchate at the Fennar.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:33.760
Through the prayers of our Holy Fathers, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.000
and save us.
